1
00:05:37,980 --> 00:05:39,880
Hey, apologies for the delay.

2
00:05:41,460 --> 00:05:42,420
There was an intruder.

3
00:05:42,820 --> 00:05:43,760
I had to shoot him.

4
00:05:44,800 --> 00:05:45,620
He's dead now.

5
00:05:45,840 --> 00:05:46,840
He's being carted off.

6
00:05:48,400 --> 00:05:49,500
Nah, I'm just messing with you.

7
00:05:49,620 --> 00:05:51,500
I had to go grab a drink and I was a little late.

8
00:05:54,490 --> 00:05:55,770
I don't know why I say that shit.

9
00:05:59,960 --> 00:06:00,940
It doesn't even make sense.

10
00:06:03,020 --> 00:06:04,540
We don't really have guns here in Denmark.

11
00:06:06,180 --> 00:06:06,580
Whoops.

12
00:06:08,160 --> 00:06:10,820
I almost broke the glass on the side of my computer just now.

13
00:06:12,700 --> 00:06:13,620
What drink you got?

14
00:06:13,860 --> 00:06:14,600
Just Coke.

15
00:06:14,820 --> 00:06:15,440
Coke Zero.

16
00:06:16,080 --> 00:06:17,320
With ice cubes.

17
00:06:18,640 --> 00:06:19,440
What about you?

18
00:06:19,820 --> 00:06:20,560
What are you drinking?

19
00:06:25,450 --> 00:06:27,130
The old man at the window has been dealt with.

20
00:06:27,250 --> 00:06:27,830
He wasn't old.

21
00:06:28,450 --> 00:06:29,750
He was quite a young guy.

22
00:06:30,990 --> 00:06:33,790
He had such a, you know, promising life ahead of him.

23
00:06:34,890 --> 00:06:36,030
Chose to waste it.

24
00:06:37,870 --> 00:06:39,630
How does it feel to touch the play button?

25
00:06:39,650 --> 00:06:40,670
Feels like...

26
00:06:42,630 --> 00:06:43,310
Touching wood.

27
00:06:44,270 --> 00:06:45,610
Because it is wood, I think.

28
00:06:46,710 --> 00:06:47,830
I was lied to.

29
00:06:48,050 --> 00:06:49,490
I thought I was gonna get silver.

30
00:06:53,100 --> 00:06:57,460
Apparently, I got the award after it became cool to get the award.

31
00:06:57,580 --> 00:06:58,340
So they changed it up.

32
00:06:58,900 --> 00:07:00,740
Apparently in the past it was actually...

33
00:07:00,740 --> 00:07:02,260
Not really silver, but like a medal, right?

34
00:07:03,540 --> 00:07:04,200
Not anymore.

35
00:07:04,660 --> 00:07:09,080
I think the center part, the actual play button in the, you know, thing is...

36
00:07:09,080 --> 00:07:10,460
Still a medal, but...

37
00:07:10,460 --> 00:07:10,520
Yeah.

38
00:07:12,940 --> 00:07:13,660
Ah, no, no.

39
00:07:13,720 --> 00:07:16,920
We're not gonna be ingesting any play buttons now that we know it's not really silver.

40
00:07:18,060 --> 00:07:20,420
The idea was to die of silver poisoning, right?

41
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:22,600
And that all goes in the drain now.

42
00:07:23,680 --> 00:07:24,160
Unfortunately.

43
00:07:25,900 --> 00:07:27,940
It does not say gym, but that would be fun.

44
00:07:32,620 --> 00:07:33,740
Did you get a diorite button?

45
00:07:33,780 --> 00:07:34,540
That would look horrible.

46
00:07:34,820 --> 00:07:36,820
I hate the look of diorite.

47
00:07:40,970 --> 00:07:42,730
It's just black and white.

48
00:07:43,090 --> 00:07:47,490
Just, you know, haphazardly thrown into the mix.

49
00:07:52,110 --> 00:07:53,290
How y'all doing today, huh?

50
00:07:54,370 --> 00:07:57,490
Are you enjoying the cold weather?

51
00:07:58,070 --> 00:07:59,510
Well, some of you, I guess.

52
00:08:02,130 --> 00:08:05,010
Did you time the background music exactly with the on-screen countdown?

53
00:08:05,610 --> 00:08:08,310
I didn't, but it always kind of works out.

54
00:08:08,490 --> 00:08:09,150
I don't know why.

55
00:08:10,050 --> 00:08:11,650
I guess the music is made that way.

56
00:08:14,700 --> 00:08:16,880
Wood is the strangest material in the universe.

57
00:08:17,060 --> 00:08:21,340
Dude, I actually saw a video just now from Kurzgesagt on wood.

58
00:08:21,400 --> 00:08:22,320
And it was very interesting.

59
00:08:22,860 --> 00:08:23,620
So you know what?

60
00:08:23,880 --> 00:08:26,700
I'm actually happy about the fact that this button is made of wood.

61
00:08:27,100 --> 00:08:30,900
There's plenty of silver out there in the universe, you know, created by supernovas and all that.

62
00:08:31,580 --> 00:08:33,700
But wood, that's very special.

63
00:08:34,200 --> 00:08:36,320
Probably only very few places in the universe.

64
00:08:36,680 --> 00:08:39,300
So far we know of one place only that produces wood.

65
00:08:40,660 --> 00:08:41,200
So boom.

66
00:08:42,740 --> 00:08:43,780
Wood superiority.

67
00:08:48,510 --> 00:08:49,770
Napoleonite, is that a real one?

68
00:08:50,930 --> 00:08:52,010
I think you're lying.

69
00:08:54,390 --> 00:08:55,150
Are we alone?

70
00:08:55,270 --> 00:08:55,730
I don't know.

71
00:08:57,850 --> 00:08:59,350
Statistically, I would say probably not.

72
00:09:03,720 --> 00:09:04,980
I would say...

73
00:09:05,520 --> 00:09:07,040
Both options are kind of crazy, right?

74
00:09:07,120 --> 00:09:07,900
Either we are alone...

75
00:09:08,760 --> 00:09:12,420
And nobody else is out there in the crazy expanse of the universe.

76
00:09:12,780 --> 00:09:13,700
There's just no way.

77
00:09:15,160 --> 00:09:16,400
And that's crazy in itself.

78
00:09:16,560 --> 00:09:17,760
That's a crazy coincidence, right?

79
00:09:17,880 --> 00:09:19,780
But if there are aliens out there...

80
00:09:20,520 --> 00:09:22,380
Then that's also insane to think about.

81
00:09:22,380 --> 00:09:23,280
That's kind of cool.

82
00:09:24,340 --> 00:09:25,400
I like both options.

83
00:09:30,590 --> 00:09:32,930
Yeah, it also makes me think of Interstellar a little bit, Cookie.

84
00:09:35,570 --> 00:09:36,310
Love that movie.

85
00:09:40,140 --> 00:09:41,020
I mean, yeah, of course.

86
00:09:41,220 --> 00:09:42,220
Intelligent life and life...

87
00:09:44,440 --> 00:09:46,220
I mean, what is intelligent life even, right?

88
00:09:47,480 --> 00:09:48,980
Nobody has a clear answer on that.

89
00:09:51,340 --> 00:09:55,060
I mean, aliens may have visited us, you know, and went, yeah, there's no intelligent life here.

90
00:09:55,380 --> 00:09:56,040
I don't know.

91
00:09:56,180 --> 00:09:57,780
Maybe it's a perspective thing.

92
00:10:02,590 --> 00:10:03,630
I don't know, Yusuf.

93
00:10:05,510 --> 00:10:06,690
I wanna see why they wouldn't be.

94
00:10:14,520 --> 00:10:15,720
Hey, thanks, Six Dagger.

95
00:10:15,980 --> 00:10:16,880
That's nice of you to say.

96
00:10:19,460 --> 00:10:20,480
I'm gonna keep winning.

97
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:23,600
Okay.

98
00:10:23,980 --> 00:10:31,160
I am actually kind of excited today because today I'm playing Ocarina of Time and I don't intend to be stuck at all.

99
00:10:31,720 --> 00:10:33,760
Today is a no-stuck stream.

100
00:10:34,500 --> 00:10:34,740
Okay?

101
00:10:35,440 --> 00:10:36,000
NSS.

102
00:10:37,140 --> 00:10:39,920
The NSS shall reign supreme.

103
00:10:43,120 --> 00:10:46,380
Because I have definitely overcome the major hurdles.

104
00:10:47,400 --> 00:10:49,220
I know how the game operates now.

105
00:10:49,900 --> 00:10:56,400
If in doubt, either show an item, play a song, do a dance, or take a swig, right?

106
00:10:56,880 --> 00:10:57,900
Those are the options.

107
00:10:58,000 --> 00:10:59,040
There's literally nothing else.

108
00:10:59,360 --> 00:11:00,900
I can't get stuck anymore.

109
00:11:02,160 --> 00:11:03,500
I can't get stuck anymore.

110
00:11:04,540 --> 00:11:05,100
Okay.

111
00:11:06,560 --> 00:11:06,920
Let's do this.

112
00:11:08,260 --> 00:11:11,160
I'm gonna... I'm gonna... transition here.

113
00:11:13,340 --> 00:11:14,480
There we go.

114
00:11:16,380 --> 00:11:17,360
Excuse me.

115
00:11:18,100 --> 00:11:20,600
Okay, I need to switch this over to stream.

116
00:11:22,140 --> 00:11:22,840
And...

117
00:11:23,560 --> 00:11:24,560
Look at that.

118
00:11:25,080 --> 00:11:25,780
Beautiful.

119
00:11:27,380 --> 00:11:28,400
Wonderful stuff.

120
00:11:30,120 --> 00:11:33,500
It's time for Link to continue his journey.

121
00:11:35,740 --> 00:11:36,760
Wait, why doesn't it work?

122
00:11:37,320 --> 00:11:37,960
Oh yeah, right!

123
00:11:38,240 --> 00:11:41,080
You click B to advance in these Nintendo games.

124
00:11:42,300 --> 00:11:44,840
My brain always reverts back to...

125
00:11:45,580 --> 00:11:47,780
You know, confirmation buttons being the X button.

126
00:11:50,660 --> 00:11:51,720
Or the A button?

127
00:11:51,880 --> 00:11:53,520
No, is it A or B on an Xbox?

128
00:11:53,700 --> 00:11:53,980
I'm not sure.

129
00:11:54,960 --> 00:11:56,020
You know what I mean.

130
00:11:56,500 --> 00:11:56,980
Uh...

131
00:11:56,980 --> 00:11:58,920
So, it seems I'm always here every time.

132
00:11:59,860 --> 00:12:01,160
What did I do last time?

133
00:12:02,260 --> 00:12:04,380
Oh, we got the boomerang-o!

134
00:12:05,960 --> 00:12:06,440
Uh...

135
00:12:07,100 --> 00:12:08,420
Look at this!

136
00:12:10,300 --> 00:12:10,780
Yoho!

137
00:12:12,620 --> 00:12:13,540
Pretty sick!

138
00:12:13,760 --> 00:12:15,220
I wonder if we can use it here for something.

139
00:12:15,220 --> 00:12:16,460
Also, you know what?

140
00:12:16,620 --> 00:12:17,440
I'm kinda curious.

141
00:12:18,280 --> 00:12:19,920
Can we go back to...

142
00:12:19,920 --> 00:12:20,860
The...

143
00:12:20,860 --> 00:12:21,860
The GDT?

144
00:12:22,380 --> 00:12:23,560
At this point in time?

145
00:12:24,980 --> 00:12:26,820
Or is that just not possible?

146
00:12:26,960 --> 00:12:27,240
Navi?

147
00:12:28,500 --> 00:12:30,560
Let's go check inside the Temple of Time!

148
00:12:31,240 --> 00:12:32,160
Navi, I'm busy.

149
00:12:33,020 --> 00:12:34,720
I'm going to check out the GDT.

150
00:12:35,740 --> 00:12:36,480
Oh shit.

151
00:12:40,790 --> 00:12:41,670
There we go.

152
00:12:42,590 --> 00:12:43,790
No problem at all.

153
00:12:46,230 --> 00:12:48,950
I think I've gotten used to not using the stick as a camera now.

154
00:12:49,070 --> 00:12:49,870
The right stick, I mean.

155
00:12:50,050 --> 00:12:51,910
I mean, I'm actually just using this button here.

156
00:12:53,990 --> 00:12:55,750
It feels natural in a weird way.

157
00:12:55,950 --> 00:12:57,190
I have been, uh...

158
00:12:57,190 --> 00:12:57,810
Converted.

159
00:12:58,770 --> 00:12:59,790
Okay, we can go inside!

160
00:13:03,370 --> 00:13:05,050
I wonder if they hide things in here now.

161
00:13:10,320 --> 00:13:11,600
Do I wanna even be in here?

162
00:13:11,900 --> 00:13:13,120
Also, can I get a better sword?

163
00:13:15,160 --> 00:13:16,340
What else did I get last time?

164
00:13:17,380 --> 00:13:18,260
We have a fish.

165
00:13:18,260 --> 00:13:20,300
We still have the, uh, Proclamation.

166
00:13:21,380 --> 00:13:23,260
And we got Farore's Wind.

167
00:13:25,320 --> 00:13:25,760
Which...

168
00:13:25,760 --> 00:13:27,380
I'm not quite sure how it works.

169
00:13:38,660 --> 00:13:41,360
Oh, that was the, uh, fast travel thingy, wasn't it?

170
00:13:41,480 --> 00:13:43,180
So if I, if I use it now...

171
00:13:45,890 --> 00:13:47,470
You cast Farore's Wind!

172
00:13:48,110 --> 00:13:49,310
Return to the warp point?

173
00:13:54,240 --> 00:13:54,680
Huh?

174
00:13:55,700 --> 00:13:56,900
That's not the warp point.

175
00:13:58,440 --> 00:13:59,000
Hold on.

176
00:14:00,360 --> 00:14:01,820
This needs to be experimented with.

177
00:14:07,680 --> 00:14:08,900
Okay, so it's made...

178
00:14:08,900 --> 00:14:11,240
Oh, so it, okay, it travels to the entrance point.

179
00:14:12,660 --> 00:14:14,400
So if I were to go up here now...

180
00:14:16,040 --> 00:14:17,880
I'm assuming I'm just gonna go back down here.

181
00:14:19,740 --> 00:14:22,560
Maybe it's like on a level-specific, uh...

182
00:14:22,560 --> 00:14:23,400
Setup, I'm not sure.

183
00:14:25,440 --> 00:14:29,260
Also, I had some trouble last time with, uh, Link not jumping across ledges properly.

184
00:14:29,940 --> 00:14:33,740
Uh, and people suggested in the comments that, uh, that could be an issue with the dead zone.

185
00:14:34,280 --> 00:14:36,480
So I played around with that on my controller a little bit.

186
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:38,220
See if it's changing anything.

187
00:14:38,320 --> 00:14:39,260
So far it's... good.

188
00:14:39,260 --> 00:14:41,040
I mean, seems to be working so far.

189
00:14:42,560 --> 00:14:45,280
Uh, let's do return to warp point and see if it works.

190
00:14:46,700 --> 00:14:47,460
Okay, yeah.

191
00:14:48,140 --> 00:14:52,360
So it looks like it's just gonna put me in the general area that I casted in.

192
00:14:53,400 --> 00:14:54,060
Good enough.

193
00:14:56,080 --> 00:14:56,520
Okay.

194
00:15:00,760 --> 00:15:03,180
Uh, I guess I wanna go to...

195
00:15:03,600 --> 00:15:04,240
The city now.

196
00:15:04,400 --> 00:15:05,980
Cause we gotta go to the Temple of Time!

197
00:15:07,440 --> 00:15:09,280
Also, I wanna go pay Zelda a visit.

198
00:15:10,540 --> 00:15:11,280
For reasons.

199
00:15:15,110 --> 00:15:16,590
So far he's jumping as he should.

200
00:15:17,710 --> 00:15:18,650
Also, what was in here?

201
00:15:22,190 --> 00:15:23,910
Ooh, we actually need a shield!

202
00:15:26,170 --> 00:15:27,830
Oh my god, I need to buy this.

203
00:15:29,250 --> 00:15:29,650
Yes!

204
00:15:34,450 --> 00:15:34,850
Nice.

205
00:15:40,610 --> 00:15:42,530
Now we can actually, uh, deflect.

206
00:15:43,930 --> 00:15:45,570
Uh, do I wanna buy anything else?

207
00:15:45,630 --> 00:15:46,210
I don't think so.

208
00:15:46,210 --> 00:15:46,910
I wanna get a bow!

209
00:15:47,210 --> 00:15:48,830
Those arrows are taunting me!

210
00:15:48,950 --> 00:15:49,610
Wait, what is that?

211
00:15:51,330 --> 00:15:52,190
Where's that on the left?

212
00:15:53,790 --> 00:15:54,910
Oh, is it seats?

213
00:15:55,570 --> 00:15:56,670
Oh, okay.

214
00:15:58,090 --> 00:15:58,610
Got it.

215
00:15:58,870 --> 00:15:59,410
I'm good.

216
00:15:59,710 --> 00:16:00,150
See you later.

217
00:16:05,390 --> 00:16:06,190
Okay, um...

218
00:16:06,190 --> 00:16:07,030
Now we go this way.

219
00:16:15,560 --> 00:16:16,800
Saria wanted to see you.

220
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:17,860
Did she find you already?

221
00:16:18,660 --> 00:16:19,560
Oh, wait, really?

222
00:16:21,220 --> 00:16:21,800
Hold up!

223
00:16:22,720 --> 00:16:24,660
Unless you're talking about something from the past here.

224
00:16:27,480 --> 00:16:28,040
Uh...

225
00:16:28,940 --> 00:16:29,500
No.

226
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:41,140
Okay, Saria.

227
00:16:42,500 --> 00:16:43,560
What do you gotta say?

228
00:16:43,760 --> 00:16:44,140
Link!

229
00:16:44,360 --> 00:16:45,520
This is Saria!

230
00:16:45,780 --> 00:16:46,380
Can you hear me?

231
00:16:47,220 --> 00:16:47,780
What?

232
00:16:48,020 --> 00:16:49,700
Your ocarina sounds...

233
00:16:49,700 --> 00:16:50,740
different somehow.

234
00:16:51,360 --> 00:16:53,260
Have you been practicing a lot, Link?

235
00:16:53,940 --> 00:16:55,100
Oh, you got me.

236
00:16:55,100 --> 00:16:57,540
I have been blowing into this thing quite a bit.

237
00:16:58,260 --> 00:16:58,620
Uh...

238
00:16:58,620 --> 00:16:59,480
I don't wanna talk again.

239
00:17:00,400 --> 00:17:00,940
We're good.

240
00:17:01,380 --> 00:17:01,880
I may...

241
00:17:01,880 --> 00:17:03,240
I'm gonna come visit you next time.

242
00:17:03,240 --> 00:17:03,860
I'm in the...

243
00:17:03,860 --> 00:17:04,940
I'm in the general area.

244
00:17:05,820 --> 00:17:06,620
Not right now, though.

245
00:17:06,640 --> 00:17:07,200
Oh, hold on.

246
00:17:08,220 --> 00:17:08,540
You!

247
00:17:08,660 --> 00:17:09,420
You troublemaker!

248
00:17:10,920 --> 00:17:11,280
Oh!

249
00:17:11,420 --> 00:17:12,060
You're okay!

250
00:17:12,600 --> 00:17:14,520
You didn't leave the forest after all, did you?

251
00:17:15,400 --> 00:17:16,160
I mean, I did.

252
00:17:16,280 --> 00:17:17,520
And then I came back, you know?

253
00:17:18,680 --> 00:17:20,260
A foreign concept, I guess.

254
00:17:23,700 --> 00:17:25,040
This is the real bad boy.

255
00:17:26,200 --> 00:17:27,280
Are you jelly now?

256
00:17:28,800 --> 00:17:29,920
Why can't I speak to you?

257
00:17:30,420 --> 00:17:31,280
Oh, I need to...

258
00:17:31,840 --> 00:17:32,240
Wait, what?

259
00:17:36,710 --> 00:17:37,450
Ah, there we go.

260
00:17:38,190 --> 00:17:42,010
If you're looking for, uh, Saria, she's in the Lost Woods as usual.

261
00:17:43,070 --> 00:17:44,890
Don't tell me you don't know where that is!

262
00:17:45,310 --> 00:17:47,830
The entrance is up on the cliff overlooking the village.

263
00:17:49,090 --> 00:17:50,290
I know you'll get lost.

264
00:17:50,510 --> 00:17:52,730
Don't worry, you'll just end up back at the entrance.

265
00:17:54,030 --> 00:17:55,730
Yeah, you would know all about that, wouldn't you?

266
00:17:57,250 --> 00:17:58,770
I shouldn't be speaking, actually.

267
00:17:58,930 --> 00:17:59,270
I...

268
00:17:59,270 --> 00:18:02,470
I've gotten lost a fair bit in there, myself.

269
00:18:03,250 --> 00:18:05,110
I can't pretend that I didn't.

270
00:18:06,010 --> 00:18:09,950
But today is gonna be a day with no getting stuck.

271
00:18:10,150 --> 00:18:11,630
We're gonna nail everything.

272
00:18:12,710 --> 00:18:16,030
Any puzzle we come across, we're gonna instantly figure it out and do it.

273
00:18:16,910 --> 00:18:19,390
Any little hiccup will instantly be resolved.

274
00:18:20,030 --> 00:18:20,690
You'll see.

275
00:18:21,510 --> 00:18:24,130
We're gonna be efficient, we're gonna be enjoying it.

276
