Am I?

560
00:33:03,890 --> 00:33:07,750
The Master Sword is a sacred blade which evil ones may never touch.

561
00:33:09,190 --> 00:33:15,490
Only one worthy of the title of Hero of Time can pull it off from the pedestal of time.

562
00:33:16,190 --> 00:33:18,510
You can call me Hot, for short.

563
00:33:19,770 --> 00:33:22,790
However, you were too young to be the hero of time.

564
00:33:24,530 --> 00:33:27,910
Therefore, your spirit was sealed here for seven years.

565
00:33:30,630 --> 00:33:31,190
What?

566
00:33:35,850 --> 00:33:41,230
And now that you're old enough, the time has come for you to awaken as the hero of time.

567
00:33:43,030 --> 00:33:45,590
Well, do you understand your destiny?

568
00:33:48,090 --> 00:33:48,770
Uh...

569
00:33:48,770 --> 00:33:49,810
Hold on.

570
00:33:50,710 --> 00:33:56,710
So I played a little song, did a silly dance, and I fell asleep for seven years?

571
00:34:00,720 --> 00:34:01,800
I understand.

572
00:34:03,560 --> 00:34:16,800
But remember, though you opened the door of time in the name of peace, Ganondorf, the Gerudo King of Thieves, used it to enter this forbidden sacred realm.

573
00:34:16,800 --> 00:34:20,060
Yeah, I remember something like that before I fell asleep.

574
00:34:21,260 --> 00:34:26,780
He obtained the Triforge from the Temple of Light, and with its power he became the King of Evil.

575
00:34:28,200 --> 00:34:36,680
His evil power radiated from the temples of Hyrule, and in seven short years, it transformed Hyrule into a world of monsters.

576
00:34:38,660 --> 00:34:39,800
Oh my god.

577
00:34:40,280 --> 00:34:44,460
My power now has only little influence, even in this sacred realm.

578
00:34:45,720 --> 00:34:47,380
Namely, this chamber of sages.

579
00:34:48,660 --> 00:34:49,980
But there is still hope.

580
00:34:50,780 --> 00:34:52,580
The power of the sages remains.

581
00:34:53,780 --> 00:35:02,400
When the power of all the sages is awakened, the sages' seals will contain all the evil power in the void of the realm.

582
00:35:03,640 --> 00:35:06,580
I, Rauru, am one of the sages.

583
00:35:07,140 --> 00:35:12,980
And your power to fight together with the sages makes you the hero of time.

584
00:35:14,460 --> 00:35:17,680
The hero of time, chosen by the Master Sword.

585
00:35:18,940 --> 00:35:20,460
Keep my spirit with you.

586
00:35:20,780 --> 00:35:25,260
And find the power of the other sages, and add their might to your own.

587
00:35:26,900 --> 00:35:27,860
Holy shit.

588
00:35:29,220 --> 00:35:30,560
That's no small ask.

589
00:35:31,980 --> 00:35:33,380
My price just went up.

590
00:35:37,820 --> 00:35:38,960
Speaking of price...

591
00:35:44,580 --> 00:35:46,420
You received the light medallion.

592
00:35:46,500 --> 00:35:47,440
Oh, I thought it was a big coin.

593
00:35:48,360 --> 00:35:50,480
Rauru the sage adds his power to yours.

594
00:35:56,600 --> 00:35:58,760
Find the other sages and save Hyrule!

595
00:36:03,940 --> 00:36:05,200
It's always me, isn't it?

596
00:36:15,750 --> 00:36:17,170
Oh my god, it's so weird.

597
00:36:21,810 --> 00:36:22,290
Link!

598
00:36:22,690 --> 00:36:24,350
We're back in the Temple of Time.

599
00:36:24,870 --> 00:36:26,810
But have seven years really passed?

600
00:36:28,630 --> 00:36:32,750
It looks like you won't be able to use some of the weapons you found as a kid anymore.

601
00:36:35,110 --> 00:36:35,990
Let's get out of here.

602
00:36:39,800 --> 00:36:40,560
Wait a minute.

603
00:36:42,460 --> 00:36:43,760
Did we travel in time?

604
00:36:46,260 --> 00:36:46,960
Time travel?

605
00:36:48,280 --> 00:36:48,680
Please.

606
00:36:53,560 --> 00:36:56,120
I've been waiting for you, hero of time.

607
00:37:00,130 --> 00:37:07,650
When evil rules all, an awakening voice from the sacred realm will call those destined to be sages, who dwell in the five temples.

608
00:37:09,490 --> 00:37:10,850
One in a deep forest.

609
00:37:11,910 --> 00:37:13,370
One on a high mountain.

610
00:37:14,590 --> 00:37:16,530
One under a vast lake.

611
00:37:17,950 --> 00:37:19,910
One within the house of the dead.

612
00:37:21,030 --> 00:37:23,570
One inside a goddess of the sand.

613
00:37:24,830 --> 00:37:31,310
Together with the hero of time, the awakened ones will bind the evil and return the light of peace to the world.

614
00:37:32,530 --> 00:37:35,890
This is the legend of the temples passed down by my people.

615
00:37:36,190 --> 00:37:36,970
The Sheikah.

616
00:37:39,390 --> 00:37:40,490
I am Sheik.

617
00:37:41,330 --> 00:37:42,570
Survivor of the Sheikahs.

618
00:37:45,380 --> 00:37:52,340
As I see you standing there holding the mythical master sword, you really do look like the legendary hero of time.

619
00:37:55,940 --> 00:37:58,740
If you believe the legend, you have no choice.

620
00:37:59,260 --> 00:38:02,420
You must look for the five temples and awaken the five sages.

621
00:38:04,480 --> 00:38:05,620
Okay, I will.

622
00:38:07,200 --> 00:38:11,320
One sage is waiting for the time of awakening in the forest temple.

623
00:38:12,040 --> 00:38:14,340
The sage is a girl I am sure you know.

624
00:38:14,340 --> 00:38:15,040
Sauria?

625
00:38:16,360 --> 00:38:21,420
Because of the evil power in the temple, she cannot hear the awakening call from the sacred realm.

626
00:38:23,460 --> 00:38:28,220
Unfortunately, equipped as you currently are, you cannot even enter the temple.

627
00:38:29,420 --> 00:38:33,840
But if you believe what I'm saying, you should head to Kakariko Village.

628
00:38:34,920 --> 00:38:36,160
Do you understand?

629
00:38:36,280 --> 00:38:36,540
Blink!

630
00:38:37,300 --> 00:38:37,880
Aha!

631
00:38:38,520 --> 00:38:39,320
I do.

632
00:38:43,720 --> 00:38:44,840
What the fuck?

633
00:38:45,040 --> 00:38:47,460
We're actually different looking.

634
00:38:47,940 --> 00:38:49,040
We are grown up.

635
00:38:51,560 --> 00:38:57,560
I'm a little confused whether or not we got put under a spell to sleep for seven years, or we traveled in time.

636
00:38:58,800 --> 00:39:05,400
I'm going to lean towards travel in time, simply because the game is called Ocarina of Time.

637
00:39:07,020 --> 00:39:07,800
Ma'am.

638
00:39:10,720 --> 00:39:13,540
To save the forest girl, you need another skill.

639
00:39:14,320 --> 00:39:15,440
Head to Kakariko Village.

640
00:39:16,680 --> 00:39:17,360
Okay.

641
00:39:18,400 --> 00:39:19,080
Okay.

642
00:39:19,940 --> 00:39:21,600
So wait a minute, what do I have?

643
00:39:22,380 --> 00:39:23,060
Oh!

644
00:39:23,400 --> 00:39:24,840
I have no slingshot anymore.

645
00:39:24,980 --> 00:39:25,840
No boomerang!

646
00:39:25,960 --> 00:39:27,220
My favorite weapon is gone.

647
00:39:28,880 --> 00:39:29,560
No!

648
00:39:30,480 --> 00:39:31,760
We have Poe.

649
00:39:32,280 --> 00:39:33,200
That's something.

650
00:39:33,720 --> 00:39:34,700
And bombs.

651
00:39:39,480 --> 00:39:39,920
What?

652
00:39:40,100 --> 00:39:40,260
Oh!

653
00:39:40,400 --> 00:39:40,460
Oh!

654
00:39:40,660 --> 00:39:41,280
Yeah, look at this.

655
00:39:41,820 --> 00:39:42,960
Now we have one of these.

656
00:39:44,480 --> 00:39:45,360
Light medallion.

657
00:39:46,000 --> 00:39:47,400
How do I use it?

658
00:39:51,000 --> 00:39:52,080
Maybe I'll figure it out.

659
00:39:53,720 --> 00:39:54,380
What's this?

660
00:39:56,020 --> 00:39:56,840
Silver scale.

661
00:39:57,120 --> 00:39:57,500
Oh yeah!

662
00:39:57,760 --> 00:39:58,860
Uh, so I can swim, right?

663
00:40:01,920 --> 00:40:03,300
Okay, so we gotta go here.

664
00:40:06,000 --> 00:40:06,800
Kakariko Village.

665
00:40:10,580 --> 00:40:12,200
Dude, seven years?

666
00:40:12,900 --> 00:40:14,000
This is crazy.

667
00:40:14,160 --> 00:40:15,100
I love time travel!

668
00:40:17,220 --> 00:40:20,160
Dude, I am a sucker for time travel stuff.

669
00:40:20,840 --> 00:40:22,200
If that's what's happening here.

670
00:40:23,840 --> 00:40:25,420
Yarkarina of time opened the door.

671
00:40:25,660 --> 00:40:28,160
The hero of time with the master sword descended here.

672
00:40:28,940 --> 00:40:31,840
Oh my god, they have like a little history about me in the past.

673
00:40:33,280 --> 00:40:34,380
It's like a museum.

674
00:40:40,330 --> 00:40:41,690
Oh shit!

675
00:40:45,840 --> 00:40:45,860
Oh shit!

676
00:40:45,860 --> 00:40:46,280
Shit!

677
00:40:46,360 --> 00:40:47,140
Shit's on fire, yo!

678
00:40:48,220 --> 00:40:48,240
Shit!

679
00:40:49,680 --> 00:40:50,980
Yeah, this is...

680
00:40:50,980 --> 00:40:51,760
This is not good.

681
00:40:54,770 --> 00:40:55,710
Uh-oh.

682
00:40:57,310 --> 00:41:00,150
What the fucking city is burned?!

683
00:41:03,320 --> 00:41:04,220
Oh, hell no.

684
00:41:08,570 --> 00:41:09,590
You ain't got nothing.

685
00:41:11,150 --> 00:41:14,190
Hey, now we can finally block with a normal shield?

686
00:41:22,040 --> 00:41:22,800
Kill them all.

687
00:41:25,080 --> 00:41:27,100
Wait a minute, what if these are actually the villagers?

688
00:41:28,780 --> 00:41:30,240
And I'm killing them all right now.

689
00:41:30,460 --> 00:41:31,180
Maybe that's a bad thing.

690
00:41:37,890 --> 00:41:40,870
Dude, I'm gone for seven years and all hell breaks loose.

691
00:41:41,730 --> 00:41:43,410
What would this kingdom do without me?

692
00:41:44,070 --> 00:41:45,310
Well, apparently nothing, it seems.

693
00:41:46,530 --> 00:41:49,430
Why are they not doing the... attack?

694
00:41:54,220 --> 00:41:55,220
Why are there so many?

695
00:41:59,380 --> 00:42:00,140
That's right.

696
00:42:00,460 --> 00:42:01,300
Can I go in here?

697
00:42:02,500 --> 00:42:03,560
This is crazy.

698
00:42:03,560 --> 00:42:04,260
I love this.

699
00:42:05,520 --> 00:42:09,140
I didn't check this building over here before I did this.

700
00:42:11,120 --> 00:42:13,020
I had a quest going on there.

701
00:42:16,220 --> 00:42:17,280
Can I go in here?

702
00:42:18,280 --> 00:42:19,400
Looks like it's open.

703
00:42:21,340 --> 00:42:22,520
That's blocked off.

704
00:42:22,720 --> 00:42:23,060
Is it?

705
00:42:24,920 --> 00:42:25,780
Yeah, it is.

706
00:42:26,860 --> 00:42:28,360
Oh, this is messed up.

707
00:42:30,120 --> 00:42:31,240
Is it also blocked?

708
00:42:32,680 --> 00:42:33,840
Oh my god.

709
00:42:37,840 --> 00:42:39,160
I'm gonna go to the castle.

710
00:43:01,900 --> 00:43:02,960
Ganon's castle?

711
00:43:02,980 --> 00:43:03,100
Ganon's castle?

712
00:43:04,880 --> 00:43:08,960
I was about to say, did the evil powers suddenly take up residence here?

713
00:43:09,480 --> 00:43:10,580
Looks like they did.

714
00:43:13,360 --> 00:43:14,720
What the hell?

715
00:43:17,520 --> 00:43:19,160
It's so weird that I'm tall.

716
00:43:22,980 --> 00:43:24,480
Even the sound is different.

717
00:43:25,160 --> 00:43:26,700
Link's voice is different.

718
00:43:28,220 --> 00:43:29,200
What is that?

719
00:43:36,340 --> 00:43:37,600
Oh, I can't hit it!

720
00:43:39,000 --> 00:43:42,360
Dude, what if I go back to the temple and play the Song of Time again?

721
00:43:44,380 --> 00:43:46,660
I wonder if this is a thing where I can go back and forth.

722
00:43:47,940 --> 00:43:49,100
Because that would be sick.

723
00:43:54,600 --> 00:43:55,840
Why didn't that break the rock?

724
00:43:55,940 --> 00:43:57,840
Okay, I guess I can just walk past the rock.

725
00:43:58,960 --> 00:43:59,860
I mean, who knows?

726
00:43:59,900 --> 00:44:01,520
Maybe there was something underneath the rock?

727
00:44:02,660 --> 00:44:04,520
Navi, you're suddenly all very quiet.

728
00:44:05,500 --> 00:44:07,480
You have nothing to say about all this?

729
00:44:10,490 --> 00:44:10,970
Grab?

730
00:44:11,110 --> 00:44:11,630
I can't grab.

731
00:44:14,610 --> 00:44:15,830
Can I grab this?

732
00:44:19,340 --> 00:44:20,180
I can't.

733
00:44:24,700 --> 00:44:26,580
Why does it say grab when I can't grab?

734
00:44:30,800 --> 00:44:32,180
Maybe if I...

735
00:44:32,180 --> 00:44:32,540
Whoa!

736
00:44:33,400 --> 00:44:34,220
Careful, Link!

737
00:44:34,440 --> 00:44:34,880
Jesus!

738
00:44:43,780 --> 00:44:45,120
What if we were to jump in here?

739
00:44:47,980 --> 00:44:49,140
Okay, I was just testing.

740
00:44:49,940 --> 00:44:51,100
It's not good for you.

741
00:44:51,460 --> 00:44:52,540
I had a feeling.

742
00:44:54,960 --> 00:44:55,880
Good thing...

743
00:44:55,880 --> 00:44:56,980
Good idea to test things, though.

744
00:45:01,250 --> 00:45:02,490
Man, that is...

745
00:45:04,290 --> 00:45:05,350
Messed up.

746
00:45:06,690 --> 00:45:07,640
Kind of mesmerizing.

747
00:45:09,850 --> 00:45:11,600
That needs to be plucked ASAP.

748
00:45:12,710 --> 00:45:13,930
With something huge.

749
00:45:15,270 --> 00:45:16,050
Look at that.

750
00:45:16,050 --> 00:45:16,910
That actually looks sick.

751
00:45:17,590 --> 00:45:18,710
Really nicely done.

752
00:45:22,440 --> 00:45:24,880
Why do evil people always have shit taste, you know?

753
00:45:24,980 --> 00:45:26,320
Why would you live in a castle like that?

754
00:45:26,400 --> 00:45:27,140
That looks like crap.

755
00:45:29,680 --> 00:45:32,360
If I was evil, I would still live in a cool-looking place.

756
00:45:32,460 --> 00:45:33,460
I wouldn't choose that place.

757
00:45:36,340 --> 00:45:37,220
Damn evil people.

758
00:45:37,380 --> 00:45:38,140
Oh, no, they're back.

759
00:45:38,300 --> 00:45:38,820
Okay, okay.

760
00:45:40,720 --> 00:45:41,580
I'm just gonna...

761
00:45:41,580 --> 00:45:42,380
I'm just gonna...

762
00:45:42,380 --> 00:45:43,740
Walk past you, if you don't mind.

763
00:45:43,960 --> 00:45:44,880
Okay, here we go with the...

764
00:45:44,880 --> 00:45:45,260
Yeah, yeah.

765
00:45:46,860 --> 00:45:48,100
The big question, though.

766
00:45:49,620 --> 00:45:50,180
Jars?

767
00:45:59,040 --> 00:45:59,600
Hello?

768
00:46:01,220 --> 00:46:01,780
Oh.

769
00:46:02,680 --> 00:46:04,980
You are quite an energetic young man.

770
00:46:05,360 --> 00:46:07,040
You're brave and handsome, too.

771
00:46:08,120 --> 00:46:08,860
Hee-hee-hee.

772
00:46:09,200 --> 00:46:10,980
Your name is Lake, isn't it?

773
00:46:11,820 --> 00:46:12,400
Hee-hee.

774
00:46:12,560 --> 00:46:13,760
Don't be surprised.

775
00:46:14,420 --> 00:46:16,100
I can read people's minds.

776
00:46:17,200 --> 00:46:20,920
If I looked as good as you, I could run a different kind of business.

777
00:46:21,440 --> 00:46:21,460
Hee-hee.

778
00:46:22,160 --> 00:46:25,060
My shop is the only ghost shop in Hyrule.

779
00:46:25,980 --> 00:46:31,320
Because of the great Ganondorf, it is a fine time for a business like this.

780
00:46:31,680 --> 00:46:31,820
Hee-hee.

781
00:46:32,580 --> 00:46:32,840
Oh!

782
00:46:33,060 --> 00:46:35,440
I can only hope the world gets even worse!

783
00:46:36,650 --> 00:46:44,140
My ghosts called Poes are spirits of concentrated hatred that appear in the fields and graveyards.

784
00:46:44,500 --> 00:46:45,700
They hate the world.

785
00:46:46,500 --> 00:46:47,340
Young man!

786
00:46:47,680 --> 00:46:51,560
If you catch a Poe, I will pay a lot of money for it!

787
00:46:51,720 --> 00:46:52,040
Hee-hee-hee-hee!

788
00:46:54,980 --> 00:46:55,820
Absolutely not.

789
00:46:56,520 --> 00:46:57,840
I will break your shit.

790
00:46:59,500 --> 00:47:03,320
Dude, I'm so tall now, I can't even horizontally slash these things anymore.

791
00:47:06,890 --> 00:47:08,110
Do I still have powers?

792
00:47:08,290 --> 00:47:08,650
Like...

793
00:47:08,650 --> 00:47:09,650
I do.

794
00:47:11,990 --> 00:47:12,470
Sweetness.

795
00:47:15,480 --> 00:47:17,460
I will find the Poes for you.

796
00:47:17,520 --> 00:47:17,900
Don't worry.

797
00:47:18,680 --> 00:47:19,300
Ooh, that's a lot of money.

798
00:47:19,400 --> 00:47:19,940
I'm maxed!

799
00:47:23,280 --> 00:47:23,720
Uh...

800
00:47:23,720 --> 00:47:25,000
What's happening today?

801
00:47:25,000 --> 00:47:26,260
If you have a Poe, I'll buy it!

802
00:47:27,360 --> 00:47:29,520
Your card now has zero points.

803
00:47:29,880 --> 00:47:30,460
Come back...

804
00:47:30,460 --> 00:47:30,940
Oh my god.

805
00:47:31,300 --> 00:47:32,620
They have visas in the future?

806
00:47:35,550 --> 00:47:36,970
I'm probably in debt as well.

807
00:47:40,150 --> 00:47:40,490
Uh...

808
00:47:42,210 --> 00:47:43,390
Okay, we can just...

809
00:47:43,390 --> 00:47:43,830
Leave.

810
00:47:45,270 --> 00:47:46,290
Wait, how did I just leave?

811
00:47:47,990 --> 00:47:49,390
I was about to say there was no bridge!

812
00:47:51,010 --> 00:47:52,030
But maybe I just...

813
00:47:52,030 --> 00:47:53,150
I mean, walk past it.

814
00:47:53,370 --> 00:47:54,050
Yeah, that makes sense.

815
00:47:55,630 --> 00:47:56,590
We can swim, right?

816
00:47:56,590 --> 00:47:57,090
That's a thing.

817
00:47:58,990 --> 00:47:59,830
Let's see the map here.

818
00:47:59,830 --> 00:48:01,130
So we gotta go to Kakariko.

819
00:48:03,610 --> 00:48:04,750
Yeah, let's just go there.

820
00:48:04,830 --> 00:48:06,750
I was about to say, but let's check out Lon Lon first!

821
00:48:07,990 --> 00:48:08,350
Uh...

822
00:48:08,350 --> 00:48:10,030
Hold on, there's something up here I wanna see real quick.

823
00:48:13,790 --> 00:48:14,950
Do we have monsters spawning?

824
00:48:22,650 --> 00:48:24,130
It is so weird that I'm tall.

825
00:48:24,530 --> 00:48:25,510
It feels wrong!

826
00:48:33,130 --> 00:48:34,490
Okay, this wall is still standing.

827
00:48:35,510 --> 00:48:36,230
Fine craftsmanship.

828
00:48:37,170 --> 00:48:39,910
I can't believe everything went to shit this fast in seven years.

829
00:48:41,170 --> 00:48:42,190
Like, what the heck?

830
00:48:42,370 --> 00:48:45,990
Also, I forgot to go back to the Temple of Time and try the melody again.

831
00:48:46,430 --> 00:48:47,350
We'll do that later.

832
00:48:47,630 --> 00:48:49,790
For now, I'm just gonna explore a little bit.

833
00:48:51,890 --> 00:48:53,790
Okay, they still have flax hanging.

834
00:48:59,170 --> 00:49:00,230
Lon Lon Rang.

835
00:49:00,330 --> 00:49:01,730
Okay, this kinda looks intact!

836
00:49:07,000 --> 00:49:07,860
Oh, okay!

837
00:49:08,380 --> 00:49:09,220
Chickens are here!

838
00:49:10,420 --> 00:49:11,420
What about upstairs?

839
00:49:19,010 --> 00:49:19,490
Oh!

840
00:49:22,010 --> 00:49:22,510
Hello!

841
00:49:27,500 --> 00:49:28,600
Stop that song!

842
00:49:28,600 --> 00:49:29,520
I...

843
00:49:29,520 --> 00:49:29,860
I...

844
00:49:31,220 --> 00:49:32,400
Oh, yeah?

845
00:49:33,540 --> 00:49:37,180
Are you talking about a specific song that rhymes with, uh...

846
00:49:37,760 --> 00:49:38,300
Verona?

847
00:49:44,580 --> 00:49:45,900
Oh, I fucked it up.

848
00:49:47,820 --> 00:49:48,680
What was it?

849
00:49:56,180 --> 00:49:57,400
Nice camera angle.

850
00:50:02,460 --> 00:50:03,760
That did nothing for you?

851
00:50:05,980 --> 00:50:07,580
Okay, what about...

852
00:50:18,350 --> 00:50:19,870
I guess a lullaby is meaningless.

853
00:50:19,870 --> 00:50:20,710
He's already sleeping.

854
00:50:22,970 --> 00:50:24,130
We're full of money.

855
00:50:24,210 --> 00:50:25,290
We don't need to be looting these.

856
00:50:26,090 --> 00:50:27,510
Unless, of course, they contain bombs.

857
00:50:28,510 --> 00:50:29,750
Also, what is going on here?

858
00:50:29,870 --> 00:50:30,750
Why is...

859
00:50:30,750 --> 00:50:32,530
Something's happening up there with the box.

860
00:50:33,070 --> 00:50:34,310
We can do something here.

861
00:50:35,270 --> 00:50:36,070
At some point.

862
00:50:36,250 --> 00:50:38,150
Also, I want my slingshot or my boomerang.

863
00:50:39,790 --> 00:50:40,810
I want it.

864
00:50:46,760 --> 00:50:47,360
Oh!

865
00:50:47,740 --> 00:50:48,320
Horses!

866
00:50:51,130 --> 00:50:52,250
Wait, do I...

867
00:50:52,250 --> 00:50:52,990
Hold on.

868
00:50:59,810 --> 00:51:00,730
Give me milk.

869
00:51:06,390 --> 00:51:07,710
What a nice song!

870
00:51:07,870 --> 00:51:09,390
It reminds me of the pasture.

871
00:51:10,230 --> 00:51:12,150
That song makes me feel so good.

872
00:51:12,150 --> 00:51:13,590
I can produce a lot of milk.

873
00:51:14,370 --> 00:51:17,030
Have some of my refreshing and nutritious milk.

874
00:51:17,830 --> 00:51:21,230
I'm glad the cow is also aware of the nutritiousness of its own milk.

875
00:51:23,750 --> 00:51:25,810
You will recover five hearts per drink.

876
00:51:26,050 --> 00:51:27,410
Or two drinks per bottle.

877
00:51:28,890 --> 00:51:29,370
Uh...

878
00:51:29,370 --> 00:51:29,650
Thank you.

879
00:51:30,710 --> 00:51:32,050
What is the bottle situation?

880
00:51:32,470 --> 00:51:33,450
We can do one more.

881
00:51:47,460 --> 00:51:48,420
There we go.

882
00:51:48,560 --> 00:51:49,000
Look at that.

883
00:51:49,900 --> 00:51:50,380
Wonderful.

884
00:51:50,980 --> 00:51:51,780
What's up, horsies?

885
00:51:52,920 --> 00:51:54,040
Do you like the melody?

886
00:51:57,450 --> 00:51:58,430
Just testing here.

887
00:52:00,030 --> 00:52:01,210
Maybe we can get a horse milk.

888
00:52:04,720 --> 00:52:06,060
Well, I guess my, uh...

889
00:52:06,060 --> 00:52:07,100
My bottles are full, right?

890
00:52:11,170 --> 00:52:11,830
Can I change...

891
00:52:11,830 --> 00:52:12,550
Oh, I can change the angle.

892
00:52:12,670 --> 00:52:12,830
Okay.

893
00:52:14,090 --> 00:52:14,570
Let's leave.

894
00:52:17,780 --> 00:52:18,300
This way.

895
00:52:22,540 --> 00:52:23,780
Oh my god, it...

896
00:52:23,780 --> 00:52:24,560
Is that Epona?

897
00:52:26,580 --> 00:52:27,360
All grown up?

898
00:52:28,580 --> 00:52:30,900
Honestly, I thought we were all already grown up last time.

899
00:52:31,100 --> 00:52:31,580
But okay.

900
00:52:36,180 --> 00:52:37,720
Oh my god, she's still standing here.

901
00:52:40,060 --> 00:52:42,900
Please keep it secret from Mr. Ingo that I sing this song.

902
00:52:44,980 --> 00:52:46,580
Hey, you remember me, right?

903
00:52:49,900 --> 00:52:50,580
Ma'am.

904
00:52:56,420 --> 00:52:57,920
Come on, you remember me now.

905
00:53:04,980 --> 00:53:05,560
You!

906
00:53:06,220 --> 00:53:07,980
Do you know my mother's song?

907
00:53:09,360 --> 00:53:11,100
Everyone really liked that song.

908
00:53:11,300 --> 00:53:13,180
My dad, even Mr. Ingo.

909
00:53:14,520 --> 00:53:18,920
But since Ganondorf appeared, Mr. Ingo has changed completely.

910
00:53:19,980 --> 00:53:23,060
I can remember the good old days only while I sing the song.

911
00:53:23,760 --> 00:53:26,880
Also, Epona really liked that song.

912
00:53:27,020 --> 00:53:27,300
What?

913
00:53:28,400 --> 00:53:29,900
Only I could tame that horse.

914
00:53:30,640 --> 00:53:31,920
Even Mr. Ingo had a hard time.

915
00:53:33,580 --> 00:53:34,700
Are you not Epona?

916
00:53:41,520 --> 00:53:42,460
Wait a minute.

917
00:53:43,960 --> 00:53:44,880
Devil's spawn!

918
00:53:45,560 --> 00:53:46,580
Devil's spawn!

919
00:53:47,060 --> 00:53:48,720
This is Ganondorf's work.

920
00:53:51,140 --> 00:53:52,340
Slice it down!

921
00:53:54,640 --> 00:53:56,060
She is evil.

922
00:53:56,240 --> 00:53:57,860
She has been replaced by an evil version.

923
00:53:58,820 --> 00:53:59,520
100%.

924
00:53:59,520 --> 00:54:03,740
Man, that little at the end there was totally a giveaway.

925
00:54:04,480 --> 00:54:06,600
This whole place is mysterious AF.

926
00:54:08,720 --> 00:54:10,220
Maybe I play another song for you.

927
00:54:14,890 --> 00:54:15,850
Let's do...

928
00:54:26,290 --> 00:54:27,090
Go to sleep.

929
00:54:30,700 --> 00:54:31,480
Epona really...

930
00:54:32,820 --> 00:54:33,760
Oh, wait a minute.

931
00:54:34,080 --> 00:54:35,300
Epona, was that the horse?

932
00:54:35,520 --> 00:54:36,720
Maybe I'm misremembering here.

933
00:54:37,780 --> 00:54:38,800
I actually forgot.

934
00:54:40,880 --> 00:54:42,460
I forgot your name, ma'am.

935
00:54:45,100 --> 00:54:46,840
Because there is no horse running around.

936
00:54:49,440 --> 00:54:49,880
Huh.

937
00:54:51,220 --> 00:54:52,600
I think I know what's happening here.

938
00:54:52,720 --> 00:54:53,620
Because that is her!

939
00:54:54,240 --> 00:54:55,020
Unless it's not.

940
00:54:55,920 --> 00:54:59,260
But let's just lean towards the idea of that is her.

941
00:54:59,460 --> 00:54:59,720
Okay?

942
00:55:00,580 --> 00:55:02,580
I take it back with the evil prediction.

943
00:55:03,120 --> 00:55:06,000
But it is kind of curious how the castle is all effed up, right?

944
00:55:06,260 --> 00:55:08,400
And then this place is all intact.

945
00:55:08,680 --> 00:55:09,480
What's up with that?

946
00:55:10,260 --> 00:55:11,360
It's right next door.

947
00:55:11,680 --> 00:55:13,060
How has this not been corrupted?

948
00:55:13,800 --> 00:55:15,180
I think it has been corrupted.

949
00:55:16,260 --> 00:55:16,740
Definitely.

950
00:55:21,320 --> 00:55:21,800
Um...

951
00:55:21,800 --> 00:55:22,180
North.

952
00:55:22,400 --> 00:55:24,100
We want to go towards the mountain now.

953
00:55:24,500 --> 00:55:24,700
Kinda.

954
00:55:25,640 --> 00:55:26,120
Kakariko.

955
00:55:27,940 --> 00:55:29,360
Dude, what if I go back home?

956
00:55:33,560 --> 00:55:34,940
We gotta check out home!

957
00:55:35,820 --> 00:55:36,400
Hold on.

958
00:55:36,560 --> 00:55:37,880
Let me contact...

959
00:55:39,420 --> 00:55:39,900
Uh...

960
00:55:39,900 --> 00:55:40,520
Contact!

961
00:55:45,460 --> 00:55:45,900
Saria!

962
00:55:46,260 --> 00:55:46,700
Saria!

963
00:55:46,700 --> 00:55:47,560
Bup, bup, bup...

964
00:55:51,950 --> 00:55:53,610
Sorry I didn't call you back for seven years.

965
00:55:58,800 --> 00:56:00,160
You want to talk to Saria, right?

966
00:56:00,820 --> 00:56:01,260
Yes!

967
00:56:02,820 --> 00:56:03,260
Link?

968
00:56:03,740 --> 00:56:05,140
Mrs. Saria, can you hear me?

969
00:56:05,860 --> 00:56:06,300
Great!

970
00:56:06,320 --> 00:56:06,940
You're safe!

971
00:56:07,320 --> 00:56:09,140
I knew I would hear from you again!

972
00:56:10,060 --> 00:56:11,400
I'm in the forest temple!

973
00:56:11,940 --> 00:56:15,100
The forest spirits were calling for help, so I went to check it out.

974
00:56:16,420 --> 00:56:18,120
But it's full of evil monsters!

975
00:56:18,480 --> 00:56:19,400
Help me, Link!

976
00:56:20,680 --> 00:56:22,700
You wanna talk to Saria again?

977
00:56:22,940 --> 00:56:23,760
Shut up, operator!

978
00:56:24,020 --> 00:56:24,420
No, I'm good.

979
00:56:25,380 --> 00:56:26,460
Okay, forest temple.

980
00:56:29,620 --> 00:56:30,020
Uh...

981
00:56:30,020 --> 00:56:31,180
Right, let me just...

982
00:56:31,180 --> 00:56:32,080
Let me just do this real quick.

983
00:56:32,240 --> 00:56:32,820
No, I don't need to.

984
00:56:33,240 --> 00:56:34,240
Maybe there's bombs, right?

985
00:56:35,860 --> 00:56:36,260
Oh!

986
00:56:36,340 --> 00:56:36,680
Navi!

987
00:56:37,960 --> 00:56:40,860
Should we believe what Sheik said and go to Kakariko Village?

988
00:56:41,600 --> 00:56:42,160
Yeah.

989
00:56:42,820 --> 00:56:43,600
We should.

990
00:56:44,160 --> 00:56:45,340
Let's go to Kakariko.

991
00:56:46,560 --> 00:56:47,320
It's fine.

992
00:56:49,800 --> 00:56:51,380
Let's go to Kakariko.

993
00:56:53,760 --> 00:56:54,480
Wait a minute.

994
00:56:55,440 --> 00:56:57,000
Why is the castle normal again?

995
00:56:57,800 --> 00:56:58,900
The eel is gone!

996
00:57:01,960 --> 00:57:03,020
Actually, not quite.

997
00:57:03,120 --> 00:57:04,560
I see the bridge is still fucked.

998
00:57:09,640 --> 00:57:10,400
It's fine.

999
00:57:18,220 --> 00:57:19,800
It's so weird being so tall.

1000
00:57:20,700 --> 00:57:22,180
The world feels smaller.

1001
00:57:25,210 --> 00:57:26,690
Oh, this place is still intact!

1002
00:57:27,870 --> 00:57:28,790
What the heck?

1003
00:57:30,150 --> 00:57:30,670
What?

1004
00:57:32,310 --> 00:57:33,490
What's happening here?

1005
00:57:34,950 --> 00:57:36,410
I tell you, I saw him!

1006
00:57:36,890 --> 00:57:40,850
I saw the ghostly figure of Dompei, the gravekeeper, sinking into his grave.

1007
00:57:40,850 --> 00:57:43,450
It looked like he was holding some kind of treasure.

1008
00:57:45,170 --> 00:57:45,930
Oh, yeah?

1009
00:57:46,530 --> 00:57:47,810
I'm gonna investigate that.

1010
00:57:48,250 --> 00:57:49,210
What about you?

1011
00:57:49,490 --> 00:57:50,370
Ha ha ha ha!

1012
00:57:51,090 --> 00:57:52,230
Look at this guy!

1013
00:57:52,530 --> 00:57:56,810
Ever since he escaped from Hyrule Castle of Town, he's become even more timid!

1014
00:57:57,670 --> 00:57:59,450
You guys are...

1015
00:57:59,970 --> 00:58:00,410
Have...

1016
00:58:00,410 --> 00:58:01,750
You've been replaced by evil!

1017
00:58:02,590 --> 00:58:04,630
I don't trust anything right now.

1018
00:58:04,930 --> 00:58:06,490
This is not normal behavior.

1019
00:58:07,450 --> 00:58:09,730
This is Ganondorf trying to act human.

1020
00:58:10,770 --> 00:58:11,990
This guy knows nothing.

1021
00:58:14,570 --> 00:58:15,010
Really?

1022
00:58:15,070 --> 00:58:16,990
As a grown-up, I don't have the strength to destroy these boxes?

1023
00:58:22,550 --> 00:58:23,230
The people...

1024
00:58:23,230 --> 00:58:24,830
Oh my god, it's the Devil Spawn Lady.

1025
00:58:25,570 --> 00:58:27,670
She was evil before the whole evil takeover.

1026
00:58:28,470 --> 00:58:31,750
All people have hardships in their past that they would rather no one found out about.

1027
00:58:33,070 --> 00:58:35,030
Look at the bearded man sleeping over there.

1028
00:58:35,510 --> 00:58:38,750
I bet even someone like him has had his share of troubles in the past.

1029
00:58:38,750 --> 00:58:40,470
You don't know his name?

1030
00:58:44,470 --> 00:58:45,110
Malon.

1031
00:58:45,630 --> 00:58:46,690
Doing alright.

1032
00:58:47,450 --> 00:58:48,750
Sorry to make you worry.

1033
00:58:49,930 --> 00:58:51,310
Oh, that's her name!

1034
00:58:52,430 --> 00:58:55,970
This is the guy who was sleeping in the castle.

1035
00:58:58,370 --> 00:58:59,990
So Malon is the kid.

1036
00:59:00,190 --> 00:59:02,210
This guy is Galon or something.

1037
00:59:02,710 --> 00:59:03,050
Talon.

1038
00:59:04,890 --> 00:59:05,530
Right?

1039
00:59:06,050 --> 00:59:07,170
Why is he here?

1040
00:59:09,070 --> 00:59:10,010
Look at him.

1041
00:59:10,010 --> 00:59:11,330
The man with the beard.

1042
00:59:11,830 --> 00:59:14,050
I think he was fired from his job at the ranch.

1043
00:59:14,790 --> 00:59:15,110
Oh.

1044
00:59:15,990 --> 00:59:17,450
He's always just lazing around.

1045
00:59:18,170 --> 00:59:19,290
Morning, noon, and night.

1046
00:59:19,690 --> 00:59:22,410
He's an awfully carefree guy during such hard times.

1047
00:59:23,910 --> 00:59:25,910
I mean, he's just sleeping, I guess.

1048
00:59:29,640 --> 00:59:30,060
Okay.

1049
00:59:35,190 --> 00:59:37,350
Oh my god, let's check out the windmill guy.

1050
00:59:39,990 --> 00:59:42,010
Yo, I bet we can hold our breath for longer, too.

1051
00:59:43,090 --> 00:59:43,710
Hey, what's up?

1052
00:59:43,750 --> 00:59:44,630
What happened to you cuckoos?

1053
00:59:45,570 --> 00:59:48,010
I bred a new type of miniature cuckoo.

1054
00:59:48,250 --> 00:59:50,150
I called it the pocket cuckoo.

1055
00:59:50,690 --> 00:59:52,510
I don't get goosebumps from this baby.

1056
00:59:53,750 --> 00:59:54,650
That's too bad.

1057
00:59:54,870 --> 00:59:56,010
Bumping geese is the best.

1058
00:59:56,890 --> 00:59:58,490
Cuckoos are very good at getting lazy.

1059
00:59:58,930 --> 01:00:00,070
Late risers out of bed.

1060
01:00:00,530 --> 01:00:01,470
Haven't you heard of them before?

1061
01:00:02,550 --> 01:00:04,310
It makes them very happy to crow.

1062
01:00:04,510 --> 01:00:04,870
Cuckoo!

1063
01:00:05,530 --> 01:00:07,590
Especially when it wakes up a very heavy sleeper.

1064
01:00:09,070 --> 01:00:10,330
Ah, I see.

1065
01:00:10,850 --> 01:00:13,630
However, my cuckoo is not entirely happy right now.

1066
01:00:14,550 --> 01:00:14,910
You?

1067
01:00:15,490 --> 01:00:17,750
You look like you're good at handling cuckoos.

1068
01:00:18,310 --> 01:00:23,570
Oh, I mean, if you remember seven years ago, I, you know, I did a little thing for you.

1069
01:00:23,730 --> 01:00:24,710
Here, take this egg.

1070
01:00:25,070 --> 01:00:29,390
After the cuckoo hatches, bring it back to me after a while and I'll check out its mood.

1071
01:00:30,230 --> 01:00:30,670
Okay.

1072
01:00:31,010 --> 01:00:31,650
What do you think?

1073
01:00:31,910 --> 01:00:32,650
Will you try?

1074
01:00:33,790 --> 01:00:34,190
Yes.

1075
01:00:37,470 --> 01:00:38,730
I'm getting deja vu here.

1076
01:00:40,770 --> 01:00:42,110
We'll hatch from it overnight.

1077
01:00:42,330 --> 01:00:43,970
Be sure to give it back when you're done with it.

1078
01:00:45,630 --> 01:00:46,030
Aha.

1079
01:00:47,230 --> 01:00:49,630
What if I let it hatch inside the man?

1080
01:00:49,790 --> 01:00:51,570
I mean, the man's house so I can wake him up.

1081
01:00:54,330 --> 01:00:55,030
Old wizard?

1082
01:00:56,290 --> 01:01:02,610
A long time ago, there was a man in this very village who had an eye they said could see the truth.

1083
01:01:03,650 --> 01:01:09,590
Now, usually, you have to train your mind's eye most strenuously to actually see the truth.

1084
01:01:10,650 --> 01:01:14,490
But this fella, no, they say he had a different way of doing things.

1085
01:01:15,410 --> 01:01:17,550
His house stood where the well is now.

1086
01:01:19,410 --> 01:01:19,930
Really?

1087
01:01:21,910 --> 01:01:23,030
You don't say.

1088
01:01:26,420 --> 01:01:28,280
I don't remember a house being here.

1089
01:01:29,600 --> 01:01:34,340
Also, the sign has gone saying the well of three descriptions or something.

1090
01:01:34,940 --> 01:01:35,620
Who are you?

1091
01:01:38,390 --> 01:01:41,110
The windmill draws water up from the depth of the well.

1092
01:01:42,070 --> 01:01:43,730
Now the well has dried up though.

1093
01:01:46,190 --> 01:01:46,590
Okay.

1094
01:01:47,190 --> 01:01:48,670
Oh shit, that means I can go down there.

1095
01:01:49,630 --> 01:01:50,490
Let's keep that in mind.

1096
01:01:51,730 --> 01:01:52,350
Good stuff.

1097
01:01:53,650 --> 01:01:55,190
I want to see the music man.

1098
01:01:59,420 --> 01:02:00,660
Oh, okay, there's a door.

1099
01:02:04,830 --> 01:02:05,710
He's still going!

1100
01:02:08,410 --> 01:02:09,150
Look at him!

1101
01:02:09,170 --> 01:02:09,190
Look at him!

1102
01:02:18,440 --> 01:02:19,820
He's my favorite character.

1103
01:02:21,160 --> 01:02:22,060
He's so good.

1104
01:02:24,300 --> 01:02:27,360
In all these years, nobody claimed the heart up top, did they?

1105
01:02:28,380 --> 01:02:28,780
Unbelievable.

1106
01:02:29,040 --> 01:02:31,020
To this tune, I could dance all night, all day!

1107
01:02:31,640 --> 01:02:32,420
I love it!

1108
01:02:33,340 --> 01:02:40,120
It gives me joy, it gives me energy, it makes me want to dance, just grab life by the balls and take it for a swing!

1109
01:02:40,920 --> 01:02:42,060
That doesn't make sense.

1110
01:02:42,240 --> 01:02:43,140
But you get the idea!

1111
01:02:45,320 --> 01:02:47,060
We should hang out, music man.

1112
01:02:48,080 --> 01:02:51,400
Is it just me or is he going even faster now than he did last time?

1113
01:02:52,420 --> 01:02:54,580
He's really working that box.

1114
01:02:55,340 --> 01:02:58,920
Also, he's holding the box in a very suspicious spot.

1115
01:02:59,160 --> 01:03:00,060
That's all I'm saying.

1116
01:03:00,680 --> 01:03:01,000
Yeah!

1117
01:03:02,360 --> 01:03:05,820
I'll never forget what happened on that day seven years ago!

1118
01:03:06,040 --> 01:03:06,340
Yeah!

1119
01:03:07,300 --> 01:03:09,140
It's all that ocarina kid's fault!

1120
01:03:09,680 --> 01:03:12,060
Next time he comes around here, I'm gonna mess him up!

1121
01:03:15,960 --> 01:03:16,360
Um...

1122
01:03:17,280 --> 01:03:18,060
Yeah, you know what?

1123
01:03:18,120 --> 01:03:19,700
I don't know anything about that.

1124
01:03:20,820 --> 01:03:21,440
I didn't...

1125
01:03:21,440 --> 01:03:22,480
I don't know anything about that.

1126
01:03:23,140 --> 01:03:24,280
I'll see you later, okay?

1127
01:03:25,620 --> 01:03:26,520
I'll see you later.

1128
01:03:27,340 --> 01:03:29,160
Maybe I'll come back and play a tune for you.

1129
01:03:30,180 --> 01:03:31,620
He apparently likes ocarinas.

1130
01:03:31,720 --> 01:03:32,800
I mean, he hates them.

1131
01:03:33,280 --> 01:03:34,600
He hates those ocarinas.

1132
01:03:36,440 --> 01:03:37,140
Let's go up here.

1133
01:03:40,230 --> 01:03:40,730
Oh!

1134
01:03:41,210 --> 01:03:41,970
No way!

1135
01:03:42,770 --> 01:03:44,770
Is that you from the castle?

1136
01:03:44,950 --> 01:03:46,890
Or not castle, but, uh, castle town.

1137
01:03:48,330 --> 01:03:49,470
Please, we'll see!

1138
01:03:49,750 --> 01:03:50,850
Please tell me something!

1139
01:03:51,070 --> 01:03:52,010
Please, we'll see!

1140
01:03:54,600 --> 01:03:55,460
What about milk?

1141
01:03:56,180 --> 01:03:56,920
Actually, hold on.

1142
01:03:56,980 --> 01:03:57,620
I'm full on money.

1143
01:03:59,140 --> 01:04:00,000
So maybe not.

1144
01:04:01,600 --> 01:04:02,100
Egg!

1145
01:04:03,980 --> 01:04:06,140
Okay, uh, what about the...

1146
01:04:06,140 --> 01:04:06,520
Hold on.

1147
01:04:06,520 --> 01:04:08,180
Maybe we can get more money now.

1148
01:04:09,600 --> 01:04:10,620
There's a house over here.

1149
01:04:15,660 --> 01:04:19,300
I don't recall if we ever, uh, destroyed more of these things.

1150
01:04:22,500 --> 01:04:22,900
Oh!

1151
01:04:25,080 --> 01:04:26,680
Please save my other brothers, too.

1152
01:04:26,880 --> 01:04:29,360
I'm sure they will give you something a lot better.

1153
01:04:30,200 --> 01:04:30,940
Will you do it?

1154
01:04:30,940 --> 01:04:32,140
I will do it.

1155
01:04:32,500 --> 01:04:33,620
Um, what about you?

1156
01:04:36,300 --> 01:04:40,260
Since you've destroyed 16 spiders of the curse, the curse is starting to weaken.

1157
01:04:41,260 --> 01:04:44,060
Did the kids who returned to normal give you any rewards?

1158
01:04:45,500 --> 01:04:50,540
You should know that the only way to become very rich is to destroy as many spiders of the curse as possible.

1159
01:04:51,780 --> 01:04:53,440
There are some tricks to finding them all.

1160
01:04:53,840 --> 01:04:55,700
First of all, you'll have to hunt at night.

1161
01:04:56,320 --> 01:04:58,200
Secondly, keep in mind that they love soft soil.

1162
01:04:59,280 --> 01:05:00,340
Pay close attention.

1163
01:05:00,940 --> 01:05:01,960
To your surroundings, please.

1164
01:05:02,260 --> 01:05:03,040
We're counting on you.

1165
01:05:03,960 --> 01:05:04,320
I...

1166
01:05:04,320 --> 01:05:05,220
Okay, uh...

1167
01:05:05,220 --> 01:05:07,260
Do I not have enough for the next stage of reward here?

1168
01:05:09,060 --> 01:05:09,420
Yeah!

1169
01:05:09,700 --> 01:05:10,400
I'm cursed!

1170
01:05:11,220 --> 01:05:11,940
Not you, eh?

1171
01:05:13,180 --> 01:05:13,780
Alright, alright.

1172
01:05:13,880 --> 01:05:14,220
What about you?

1173
01:05:15,980 --> 01:05:16,840
You're also cursed.

1174
01:05:17,020 --> 01:05:17,840
Everyone's cursed in here.

1175
01:05:19,680 --> 01:05:20,040
Oh.

1176
01:05:20,400 --> 01:05:21,200
Oh, didn't mean to do that.

1177
01:05:21,760 --> 01:05:22,680
I'll be back later.

1178
01:05:23,260 --> 01:05:23,620
Wait a minute.

1179
01:05:23,920 --> 01:05:24,680
Do you guys want X?

1180
01:05:28,110 --> 01:05:29,910
Okay, we gotta use it overnight or whatever.

1181
01:05:30,370 --> 01:05:30,870
Make it hatch.

1182
01:05:30,990 --> 01:05:32,410
And then we gotta wake that guy up in the house.

1183
01:05:33,810 --> 01:05:34,890
Are you gonna say anything new?

1184
01:05:37,290 --> 01:05:37,970
No, okay.

1185
01:05:42,600 --> 01:05:43,000
Beautiful.

1186
01:05:43,620 --> 01:05:44,240
Let's head up here.

1187
01:05:50,050 --> 01:05:50,850
Inside we go.

1188
01:05:54,180 --> 01:05:57,160
I'm surprised how many people are just sort of going about their business.

1189
01:05:57,680 --> 01:05:59,980
I thought the world would be all messed up, you know?

1190
01:06:00,820 --> 01:06:01,240
Hey, young man!

1191
01:06:01,360 --> 01:06:04,880
A grown boy like you entering a person's house without permission?

1192
01:06:05,500 --> 01:06:06,840
I want to talk to your parents.

1193
01:06:07,140 --> 01:06:08,280
Hey, I'm not a boy anymore.

1194
01:06:08,860 --> 01:06:09,460
Oh, well.

1195
01:06:10,240 --> 01:06:11,660
This isn't my house anyway.

1196
01:06:12,100 --> 01:06:13,480
This is the great Impa's house.

1197
01:06:13,900 --> 01:06:14,340
Yeah, I know.

1198
01:06:14,780 --> 01:06:18,300
The great Impa has gone to the graveyard to seal up the humongous creature there.

1199
01:06:19,180 --> 01:06:19,620
What?

1200
01:06:20,360 --> 01:06:23,520
Since Ganondorf appeared, many monsters have been sighted around here.

1201
01:06:24,400 --> 01:06:26,760
Only the great Impa has kept peace in our village.

1202
01:06:27,280 --> 01:06:28,900
You have to remember that, young man.

1203
01:06:29,780 --> 01:06:30,460
Oh, well.

1204
01:06:31,520 --> 01:06:34,120
Speaking of the great Impa, she hasn't come back yet.

1205
01:06:34,580 --> 01:06:35,680
I wonder what happened to her.

1206
01:06:36,640 --> 01:06:41,500
I heard that the ghost of the gravekeeper often appears in the graveyard behind this village.

1207
01:06:42,220 --> 01:06:43,480
But, no big deal.

1208
01:06:44,380 --> 01:06:44,820
Okay.

1209
01:06:45,760 --> 01:06:47,600
Yeah, that ghost is not really scary.

1210
01:06:47,600 --> 01:06:48,480
I'm not scared of him.

1211
01:06:49,860 --> 01:06:51,740
He used to, uh...

1212
01:06:51,740 --> 01:06:55,440
You know, he used to be my booker, whatever you call it, in terms of gambling.

1213
01:06:56,340 --> 01:06:58,580
He would, uh, place my bets, you know?

1214
01:06:58,980 --> 01:07:00,240
and collect the money for me.

1215
01:07:02,180 --> 01:07:03,600
He's a good guy, this Dampe.

1216
01:07:04,180 --> 01:07:04,840
I love him.

1217
01:07:06,760 --> 01:07:09,860
But, uh, let's go put a damper on his charade here.

1218
01:07:10,340 --> 01:07:11,140
Didn't need to speak to you.

1219
01:07:12,040 --> 01:07:12,460
So, hold on.

1220
01:07:12,520 --> 01:07:13,000
It's day now.

1221
01:07:14,740 --> 01:07:16,040
Wait, has it been day the entire time?

1222
01:07:16,120 --> 01:07:16,600
Maybe it has been.

1223
01:07:18,340 --> 01:07:19,380
We gotta find a chicken.

1224
01:07:20,220 --> 01:07:20,620
Oh, wait.

1225
01:07:20,660 --> 01:07:21,080
We have a chicken.

1226
01:07:21,260 --> 01:07:22,580
Uh, we gotta grow it up.

1227
01:07:23,300 --> 01:07:23,780
Raise it.

1228
01:07:24,480 --> 01:07:24,880
Hatch it.

1229
01:07:25,340 --> 01:07:26,140
You know what I mean.

1230
01:07:27,200 --> 01:07:27,780
Graveyard time.

1231
01:07:30,780 --> 01:07:32,620
The problem is, we may have to come back at night.

1232
01:07:35,560 --> 01:07:39,280
Uh, here lie the souls of those who swore fealty to the royal family of Hyrule.

1233
01:07:40,220 --> 01:07:45,340
The Sheikah, guardians of the royal family and founders of Kakariko watch over these spirits in their eternal slumber.

1234
01:07:46,940 --> 01:07:47,720
That's the same.

1235
01:07:49,700 --> 01:07:50,800
His house is still here.

1236
01:07:51,840 --> 01:07:53,260
Let's see what he wrote in his diary.

1237
01:07:54,860 --> 01:07:56,400
The gravekeeper's diary is here.

1238
01:07:56,520 --> 01:07:57,380
Do you wanna read it?

1239
01:07:57,720 --> 01:07:58,140
Yes.

1240
01:07:59,280 --> 01:08:01,060
Whoever reads this, please enter my grave.

1241
01:08:01,060 --> 01:08:03,760
I will let you have my stretching, shrinking keepsake.

1242
01:08:04,160 --> 01:08:04,620
Huh?

1243
01:08:05,740 --> 01:08:06,780
I'm waiting for you.

1244
01:08:06,980 --> 01:08:07,260
Damping.

1245
01:08:09,720 --> 01:08:11,060
What are you on about?

1246
01:08:17,020 --> 01:08:18,840
Stretching, sinking, keepsake?

1247
01:08:20,820 --> 01:08:21,140
Bruh.

1248
01:08:25,810 --> 01:08:26,130
Boom.

1249
01:08:30,260 --> 01:08:31,200
Is this the right one, though?

1250
01:08:31,280 --> 01:08:31,560
Oh, look!

1251
01:08:31,640 --> 01:08:32,480
The chest is still open.

1252
01:08:34,640 --> 01:08:35,500
Now I'm grown up, though.

1253
01:08:35,500 --> 01:08:36,260
I'm not scared of anything.

1254
01:08:37,980 --> 01:08:38,440
Oh, wait.

1255
01:08:38,500 --> 01:08:40,260
This is not the place I thought it was.

1256
01:08:43,300 --> 01:08:43,620
Egg?

1257
01:08:46,120 --> 01:08:46,620
No egg.

1258
01:08:47,260 --> 01:08:49,400
I'm not sure what these, uh, spirits do.

1259
01:08:55,980 --> 01:08:56,300
Oh.

1260
01:08:59,900 --> 01:09:00,960
Okay, so it's not this one.

1261
01:09:06,590 --> 01:09:07,410
Oh, is that a hole?

1262
01:09:08,550 --> 01:09:09,490
Oh, it looked like a hole.

1263
01:09:11,650 --> 01:09:13,630
Maybe I can find a shovel and dig myself.

1264
01:09:18,170 --> 01:09:19,110
Oh, here they come.

1265
01:09:25,780 --> 01:09:26,100
Wait.

1266
01:09:26,720 --> 01:09:28,580
I guess my sword is stronger, right?

1267
01:09:28,600 --> 01:09:29,400
That was only two hits.

1268
01:09:30,400 --> 01:09:31,600
That used to take way more.

1269
01:09:34,860 --> 01:09:35,840
Oh, there's someone up here.

1270
01:09:37,100 --> 01:09:37,920
What the?

1271
01:09:38,780 --> 01:09:39,360
Oh!

1272
01:09:39,940 --> 01:09:40,540
Ah!

1273
01:09:43,530 --> 01:09:44,130
Okay.

1274
01:09:45,470 --> 01:09:47,410
There's multiple places I want to enter.

1275
01:09:48,430 --> 01:09:49,870
Uh, unfortunately, we...

1276
01:09:49,870 --> 01:09:50,570
What did I just do?

1277
01:09:51,970 --> 01:09:52,690
That's fine.

1278
01:09:56,860 --> 01:09:58,640
You defeated Poe the ghost.

1279
01:09:59,540 --> 01:10:00,560
You want to catch in a...

1280
01:10:00,560 --> 01:10:01,480
Uh, I actually do!

1281
01:10:02,280 --> 01:10:03,100
No, no, no!

1282
01:10:03,620 --> 01:10:03,940
Oh!

1283
01:10:04,960 --> 01:10:05,800
You shouldn't disappear.

1284
01:10:06,920 --> 01:10:11,480
I was going to drink the milk and then put it in the empty bottle so I can bring it back to the one that wants it.

1285
01:10:13,540 --> 01:10:14,380
Let's check this out again.

1286
01:10:15,740 --> 01:10:18,040
I don't think it's down here, but let's just check it out anyway.

1287
01:10:24,960 --> 01:10:26,240
Shine light on the living dead.

1288
01:10:27,440 --> 01:10:29,020
What about the thing I just got?

1289
01:10:29,160 --> 01:10:30,060
Wasn't that something light?

1290
01:10:32,140 --> 01:10:32,780
Light medallion!

1291
01:10:34,420 --> 01:10:34,840
Oh, yeah.

1292
01:10:35,000 --> 01:10:35,660
I guess we can save.

1293
01:10:37,040 --> 01:10:39,440
How do I actually light...

1294
01:10:45,880 --> 01:10:47,640
I can't equip it.

1295
01:10:54,530 --> 01:10:54,970
What?

1296
01:10:55,430 --> 01:10:56,110
Greg?

1297
01:10:58,710 --> 01:10:59,630
What does that mean?

1298
01:11:00,810 --> 01:11:02,130
Well, how did I just do that?

1299
01:11:04,710 --> 01:11:05,150
What?

1300
01:11:07,490 --> 01:11:08,730
Sure, save.

1301
01:11:10,090 --> 01:11:10,850
Greg?

1302
01:11:11,630 --> 01:11:12,750
Who's Greg?

1303
01:11:14,450 --> 01:11:15,930
I don't understand what just happened.

1304
01:11:16,030 --> 01:11:17,030
How do I use this medallion?

1305
01:11:21,560 --> 01:11:25,760
Those who break into the royal tomb will be obstructed by the lurkers in the dark.

1306
01:11:26,000 --> 01:11:26,400
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

1307
01:11:27,620 --> 01:11:28,020
Okay.

1308
01:11:31,210 --> 01:11:32,190
Okay, let's go up here.

1309
01:11:36,010 --> 01:11:38,710
I hope I didn't miss anything with the light medallion.

1310
01:11:40,170 --> 01:11:41,550
Okay, these guys are still here to see.

1311
01:11:41,790 --> 01:11:42,150
Oh!

1312
01:11:44,430 --> 01:11:45,090
Oh, God.

1313
01:11:46,410 --> 01:11:46,990
Piss off!

1314
01:11:47,850 --> 01:11:49,070
Dude, get off of me!

1315
01:11:50,870 --> 01:11:51,670
Oh, man!

1316
01:11:53,990 --> 01:11:54,390
Ugh!

1317
01:11:56,870 --> 01:11:58,490
Okay, you really gotta kill them, I guess.

1318
01:12:01,150 --> 01:12:01,550
Assholes.

1319
01:12:07,560 --> 01:12:10,120
The poem is dedicated to the memory of the dearly departed.

1320
01:12:10,740 --> 01:12:11,700
This is the same.

1321
01:12:14,080 --> 01:12:14,600
All right.

1322
01:12:15,920 --> 01:12:16,780
Oh, oh, wait.

1323
01:12:16,780 --> 01:12:18,100
I can just play the sun song, right?

1324
01:12:18,100 --> 01:12:19,520
What is...

1325
01:12:19,520 --> 01:12:20,360
Dude, what is this?

1326
01:12:22,020 --> 01:12:23,820
How do I...

1327
01:12:23,820 --> 01:12:25,000
What?

1328
01:12:26,540 --> 01:12:28,220
I am so confused by that.

1329
01:12:32,740 --> 01:12:33,320
Greg.

1330
01:12:34,740 --> 01:12:35,380
Oh.

1331
01:12:35,900 --> 01:12:36,840
Oh, okay.

1332
01:12:37,600 --> 01:12:39,300
So I can change it like that.

1333
01:12:40,040 --> 01:12:41,320
Can I change the other screens?

1334
01:12:43,960 --> 01:12:44,640
That's weird.

1335
01:12:46,120 --> 01:12:47,260
I don't know what that is.

1336
01:12:50,120 --> 01:12:50,540
No.

1337
01:12:50,820 --> 01:12:51,400
Don't save now.

1338
01:12:52,820 --> 01:12:55,000
I'm messing around in the menus a little too much here.

1339
01:12:55,160 --> 01:12:57,100
Okay, so the song I'm looking for is the sun one.

1340
01:12:57,760 --> 01:12:58,120
That one.

1341
01:12:58,800 --> 01:12:58,980
Down.

1342
01:12:59,460 --> 01:13:00,420
Right down, up.

1343
01:13:01,560 --> 01:13:04,200
We gotta equip the music maker.

1344
01:13:06,440 --> 01:13:07,640
Right down, up.

1345
01:13:16,180 --> 01:13:16,880
Okay.

1346
01:13:20,820 --> 01:13:21,940
There we go.

1347
01:13:23,440 --> 01:13:24,980
See you later, nerds.

1348
01:13:31,360 --> 01:13:32,080
Okay.

1349
01:13:36,710 --> 01:13:37,610
Let's go.

1350
01:13:39,170 --> 01:13:41,070
I wanna pull all the graves now.

1351
01:13:45,460 --> 01:13:47,420
Notice how it's also raining just up here.

1352
01:13:47,600 --> 01:13:49,760
But if you go a little further down, it's not raining anymore.

1353
01:13:50,700 --> 01:13:51,060
Isn't that weird?

1354
01:13:54,140 --> 01:13:55,280
Like, here it's not raining.

1355
01:14:02,480 --> 01:14:04,220
Does this guy even wanna mess with me?

1356
01:14:05,480 --> 01:14:05,840
Nope.

1357
01:14:05,980 --> 01:14:06,400
He doesn't care.

1358
01:14:12,570 --> 01:14:13,170
Oh, wait a minute.

1359
01:14:13,190 --> 01:14:14,250
There's flowers in this one now.

1360
01:14:17,480 --> 01:14:18,400
Oh, that's new.

1361
01:14:19,520 --> 01:14:20,100
Down we go.

1362
01:14:23,080 --> 01:14:24,100
Oh, shit.

1363
01:14:24,100 --> 01:14:24,940
There he is.

1364
01:14:26,540 --> 01:14:27,940
Haha, young man.

1365
01:14:28,520 --> 01:14:29,960
Are you fast on your feet?

1366
01:14:31,060 --> 01:14:33,720
I may not look like it, but I'm confident in my speed.

1367
01:14:34,160 --> 01:14:35,060
Let's have a race.

1368
01:14:35,660 --> 01:14:36,460
Follow me if you dare.

1369
01:14:37,560 --> 01:14:38,160
Oh, yeah?

1370
01:14:39,780 --> 01:14:40,400
Oh, wow.

1371
01:14:44,820 --> 01:14:45,640
I'm so ready.

1372
01:14:46,960 --> 01:14:48,080
You ain't got nothing on me.

1373
01:14:58,140 --> 01:14:58,540
Wow.

1374
01:14:59,820 --> 01:15:00,340
Oh, no.

1375
01:15:00,440 --> 01:15:00,840
He went right.

1376
01:15:01,260 --> 01:15:01,780
Ah, shit.

1377
01:15:03,240 --> 01:15:03,640
